From 3805730e0b065fba9ec5f615fe4c7dde16d847a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:32:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/52] kt-ep hybrid: compact CPU-expert view, kt-kernel 0.7
 API, fixes for V4.1-Flash MXFP4

- KTEPWrapperMethod.fuse_routed_scaling_factor_in_topk = False: stops the
  routed_scaling_factor (1.5) being applied twice via __getattr__ leak.
- Compact CPU view: patched MXFP4SafeTensorLoader.load_experts returns only
  the CPU-resident experts renumbered 0..n_cpu-1, so kt-kernel repacks
  3.4 GiB/layer instead of 8.3 GiB (kt-kernel packs all num_experts
  regardless of gpu_experts_mask). Requires identity physical->logical map.
- remap_topk_ids_for_cpu(): GPU slots -> -1 (kt skip marker), CPU ids
  shifted by num_gpu_experts, out of place before mask_cpu_expert_ids.
- KTMoEWrapper(num_experts=n_cpu, gpu_experts_mask=None,
  swiglu_limit=moe_runner_config.swiglu_limit) matches kt-kernel 0.7.0.post4.
- All-GPU layer guard (num_gpu_experts >= num_experts): no KT wrapper.
- mxfp4_flashinfer_cutlass_moe: size per-expert tensors from w13_weight.
- decode_cuda_graph_runner: set_capture_batch_sizes on token counts
  (bs * captured_req_width), which is what kt-kernel keys buffers on.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
